# <type>(<scope>): <imperative summary>
#
# Subject:
# - Describe one coherent outcome in imperative English.
# - Use an allowed type and the narrowest stable Cycles scope.
# - Avoid file lists, vague status words, and trailing punctuation.
#
# Standard body:
#
# Why:
# - State the confirmed problem, requirement, invariant, or measured bottleneck.
#
# Changes:
# - Describe observable behavior and the responsibility that now owns it.
# - Include the relevant failure, reset, fallback, or cleanup path.
#
# Validation:
# - PASS `<command or suite>` — state the variant and what it proved.
# - KNOWN RED `<command or suite>` — name the earliest failing domain.
# - NOT RUN `<check>` — state the exact reason.
# - Use repository-relative evidence; omit secrets, private paths, and raw logs.
#
# High-risk additions for ABI, native lifecycle, Vulkan/CUDA interop, shaders,
# settings, resources, devices, frame transport, or runtime compatibility:
#
# Contracts:
# - ABI / layouts: <version, size, offsets, enums, flags, rejection behavior>
# - Ownership / lifecycle: <thread, handle, lease, generation, reset, close>
# - Settings / resources: <keys, IDs, defaults, formats, pipeline order>
#
# Variants / Backends:
# - <default | DLSS> / <OPTIX | CUDA | CPU> — <result or exclusion reason>
#
# Compatibility / Risks:
# - State migration, fallback, upstream revision, packaging, and rollback.
#
# Runtime evidence:
# - PASS `<Minecraft workflow>` — include backend, device, mode, and observation.
# - NOT RUN `<workflow>` — state the exact reason.
#
# Known limitations:
# - Name remaining red domains without claiming partial work is complete.
#
# Stage:
# - <stage document or independently verifiable stage>
#
# Optional footers (only when true):
# Refs: <issue, contract, upstream revision, or authoritative document>
# Reverts: <full commit hash>
# BREAKING CHANGE: <consumer impact, rejection behavior, and migration>
# Co-authored-by: <actual contributor name> <verified email>
#
# Allowed types:
# feat fix perf refactor test docs build ci chore revert
#
# Common scopes:
# render scene native abi interop vulkan camera sampling denoiser color hdr pbr
# material texture config ui mixin runtime diagnostics cycles offline build patch
# repo docs
#
# Remove unused sections. Never report PASS for a check that was not run.
# See docs/commit-conventions.md for message levels and Cycles-specific rules.
